# Cloudflare Workers static assets reads this file from the root of the assets
# directory. It is the ONLY mechanism this site has for setting response
# headers, and that is deliberate: ADR-0001 chose static assets with no Worker
# code partly because Cloudflare documents that "custom headers defined in the
# `_headers` file are not applied to responses generated by your Worker code",
# so a Worker would silently break the policy below.
#
# Two documented traps are at work here (ADR-0004 Decision 5):
#
#   1. Every matching rule applies, and a header set twice is comma-joined.
#      Two `Cache-Control` values become one invalid-looking list, and two
#      `Content-Security-Policy` values become two policies that the browser
#      intersects. `! Header-Name` detaches an inherited header so a narrower
#      rule can set it cleanly. Every override below detaches first.
#   2. Limits are 100 rules per file and 2000 characters per line including the
#      header name. The CSP line below is 290 characters; keep it inside the
#      limit by letting Subresource Integrity carry the hashes instead of the
#      policy.
#
# Every comment in this file sits at column 0 and never inside a rule body.
# Cloudflare documents `#` comments for this format but says nothing about an
# indented one, and a comment mis-parsed as a header name would break the CSP
# silently. `make web-serve` serves ./dist with these exact rules applied, so
# the policy can be read off a real response locally; `astro preview` sends
# none of them.
#
# Tested against a real build (web/README.md): the page mounts, the worker
# starts, a preview renders and a PDF downloads with no violation reported.
# `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` is required for WebAssembly and `'unsafe-eval'` is
# deliberately NOT paired with it — that would re-enable eval() for every
# visitor in order to support engines older than Safari 16.
# `connect-src 'self'` is the line a reviewer is meant to read, and it is
# evidence about intent rather than a seal on the origin: CSP has no shipped
# directive restricting top-level navigation.
#
# `Integrity-Policy: blocked-destinations=(script)` makes integrity metadata
# MANDATORY for script requests, which closes the hole where an attacker who
# can rewrite the HTML simply deletes the `integrity` attributes. It is only
# shippable because `make web-build` runs `scripts/web-attest.py`, which emits
# a `modulepreload` link carrying a hash for every chunk the entry script
# imports. MEASURED: with the header and without those links, the chunk request
# is blocked outright and the application is blank. With them, the page mounts
# and a tampered chunk is refused. Deploying a `dist/` that has not been
# attested therefore ships a blank page — which is why `make web-deploy-check`
# runs the verifier before anything is uploaded.
#
# `Cache-Control` here is stated rather than inherited. Cloudflare's own
# default for static assets happens to be the same value, but a platform
# default is not a decision we have recorded.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; manifest-src 'none'; media-src 'none'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Integrity-Policy: blocked-destinations=(script)
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Content-addressed, so a URL's bytes never change and an old HTML keeps
# resolving to the bytes its `integrity` attribute names. That is what makes
# Cloudflare's "HTML and its assets may come from different versions" mid-
# rollout survivable under Subresource Integrity, which fails closed on a
# mismatch.

/_pochoir/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The compiled engine. `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` rejects anything
# whose Content-Type is not exactly `application/wasm`, so this is stated
# rather than left to extension sniffing. The engine gets its own directory so
# that the rule can use a trailing splat, which is the only pattern form
# Cloudflare documents; `/_pochoir/*` also matches these paths, which is why
# both headers are detached before being set again.

/_pochoir/engine/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  ! Content-Type
  Content-Type: application/wasm
